        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 86-year-old male admitted under our care for an acute exacerbation of his known Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray was performed to exclude pneumonia and pneumothorax. Spirometry confirmed severely reduced airflow. Blood gases revealed mild hypoxaemia. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators including salbutamol and ipratropium, a course of systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. He responded satisfactorily to treatment with improved respiratory function and oxygen saturation. He is discharged in stable condition and I recommend close follow-up of his COPD management, inhaler technique review, and optimisation of his maintenance therapy. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
